<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Parent app entitlements. Deliberately almost empty: the parent device enforces
  NOTHING. No family-controls, no networkextension — this app is a client of the
  API, and asking for filtering entitlements it never uses would be a claim to
  justify at App Review for no capability.

  Push arrives when APNs is actually wired; the entitlement is inert until code
  registers for remote notifications (docs/APPLE_ACCOUNT_SETUP.md §4.1 C).

  The macOS destination is sandboxed and needs outgoing network explicitly.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Passkeys. `ASAuthorizationPlatformPublicKeyCredentialProvider` will only
      produce an assertion for a relying party this app is entitled to, and the
      rpId is the apex (backend/wrangler.toml PASSKEY_RP_ID).

      This is HALF of the requirement. The other half is an
      apple-app-site-association served from https://ajar.family listing this
      app id, which the API router serves from APPLE_APP_IDS. Either one
      missing produces the same opaque failure, so App/Passkeys.swift maps it to
      copy that points the parent at the browser instead.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>webcredentials:ajar.family</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
